// Siegfried, Act 3: complete public-domain German and machine-assisted English working translation.
export const siegfriedAct3Scenes = [{"number":1,"originalHeading":"ERSTE SZENE","translatedHeading":"First Scene","summary":"","sections":[{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Wache, Wala! Wala! Erwach'!","translatedTitle":"Wake up, Wala! Wala! Awake!","participants":["WANDERER","ERDA"],"sourceStartIndex":0,"sourceLineCount":71,"turns":[{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Wilde Gegend, am Fusse eines Felsenberges, welcher links nach hinten steil aufsteigt. Nacht, Sturm und Wetter, Blitz und heftiger Donner, welch letzterer dann schweigt, während Blitze noch längere Zeit die Wolken durchkreuzen\nWanderer, Erda\nschreitet entschlossen auf ein gruftähnliches Höhlentor in einem Felsen des Vordergrundes zu und nimmt dort, auf seinen Speer gestützt, eine Stellung ein, während er das Folgende dem Eingange der Höhle zu ruft","translation":"A wild area, at the foot of a rocky mountain that rises steeply to the left. Night, storm and weather, lightning and violent thunder, the latter then falling silent, while lightning continues to crisscross the clouds for some time.\nWanderer, Erda\nHe strides resolutely towards a crypt-like cave entrance in a rock in the foreground and, leaning on his spear, takes up a position there, while shouting the following towards the entrance of the cave.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":0,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Wache, Wala! Wala! Erwach'!\nAus langem Schlaf weck' ich dich Schlummernde wach.\nIch rufe dich auf: Herauf! Herauf!\nAus nebliger Gruft,\naus nächtigem Grunde herauf!\nErda! Erda! Ewiges Weib!\nAus heimischer Tiefe tauche zur Höh!\nDein Wecklied sing' ich, dass du erwachest;\naus sinnendem Schlafe weck' ich dich auf.\nAllwissende! Urweltweise!\nErda! Erda! Ewiges Weib!\nWache, erwache, du Wala! Erwache!","translation":"Wake up, Wala! Wala! Awake!\nFrom your long sleep I awaken you, slumbering one.\nI call to you: Up! Up!\nFrom a misty tomb,\nup from the depths of night!\nEarth! Earth! Eternal Woman!\nFrom the depths of my homeland, I dive to the heights!\nI sing your wake-up song so that you may awaken;\nI will awaken you from your pensive sleep.\nAll-knowing! Ancient sages!\nEarth! Earth! Eternal Woman!\nWake up, awaken, you Wala! Awake!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":3,"sourceLineCount":12},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Die Höhlengruft erdämmert. Bläulicher Lichtschein: von ihm beleuchtet steigt mit dem Folgenden Erda sehr allmählich aus der Tiefe auf. Sie erscheint wie von Reif bedeckt: Haar und Gewand werfen einen glitzernden Schimmer von sich","translation":"The cavernous crypt is dim. A bluish light illuminates the space, and Erda, following it, gradually rises from the depths. She appears as if covered in frost: her hair and garments cast a glittering shimmer.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":15,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"ERDA","speakerTranslation":"ERDA","original":"Stark ruft das Lied;\nkräftig reizt der Zauber.\nIch bin erwacht aus wissendem Schlaf:\nwer scheucht den Schlummer mir?","translation":"The song calls out loudly;\nThe magic is powerfully alluring.\nI have awakened from a knowing sleep:\nWho will chase away my slumber?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":16,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Der Weckrufer bin ich, und Weisen üb' ich,\ndass weithin wache, was fester Schlaf verschliesst.\nDie Welt durchzog ich,\nwanderte viel, Kunde zu werben,\nurweisen Rat zu gewinnen.\nKundiger gibt es keine als dich;\nbekannt ist dir, was die Tiefe birgt,\nwas Berg und Tal, Luft und Wasser durchwebt.\nWo Wesen sind, wehet dein Atem;\nwo Hirne sinnen, haftet dein Sinn:\nalles, sagt man, sei dir bekannt.\nDass ich nun Kunde gewänne,\nweck' ich dich aus dem Schlaf!","translation":"I am the wake-up caller, and I practice wisdom,\nthat which is widely awake, while deep sleep closes it off.\nI traveled the world,\nwandered a lot to attract customers,\nTo gain wise counsel.\nThere is no one more knowledgeable than you;\nYou know what the depths hold,\nwhich interweaves mountain and valley, air and water.\nWhere beings are, your breath blows;\nWhere minds ponder, your senses adhere:\nThey say you know everything.\nThat I would now gain customers,\nI'll wake you up from your sleep!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":20,"sourceLineCount":13},{"speaker":"ERDA","speakerTranslation":"ERDA","original":"Mein Schlaf ist Träumen,\nmein Träumen Sinnen,\nmein Sinnen Walten des Wissens.\nDoch wenn ich schlafe,\nwachen Nornen:\nsie weben das Seil\nund spinnen fromm, was ich weiss.\nWas frägst du nicht die Nornen?","translation":"My sleep is dreaming,\nmy dreams, thoughts,\nMy senses govern the power of knowledge.\nBut when I sleep,\nThe Norns are awake:\nThey weave the rope\nand spin piously, as far as I know.\nWhy don't you ask the Norns?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":33,"sourceLineCount":8},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Im Zwange der Welt weben die Nornen:\nsie können nichts wenden noch wandeln.\nDoch deiner Weisheit\ndankt' ich den Rat wohl,\nwie zu hemmen ein rollendes Rad?","translation":"The Norns weave within the constraints of the world:\nThey cannot change or transform anything.\nBut of your wisdom\nI thanked the advice well,\nHow do you stop a rolling wheel?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":41,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"ERDA","speakerTranslation":"ERDA","original":"Männertaten umdämmern mir den Mut:\nmich Wissende selbst\nbezwang ein Waltender einst.\nEin Wunschmädchen gebar ich Wotan:\nder Helden Wal\nhiess für sich er sie küren.\nKühn ist sie und weise auch:\nwas weckst du mich und frägst um Kunde\nnicht Erdas und Wotans Kind?","translation":"Men's deeds shake my courage:\nI, the knowledgeable one, myself\nA ruler once defeated him.\nI bore Wotan a girl he had wished for:\nthe hero's whale\nFor him, that meant choosing them.\nShe is bold and wise too:\nWhy are you waking me up and asking for a customer?\nNot Erda's and Wotan's child?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":46,"sourceLineCount":9},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Die Walküre meinst du,\nBrünnhild', die Maid?\nSie trotzte dem Stürmebezwinger,\nwo er am stärksten selbst sich bezwang:\nwas den Lenker der Schlacht zu tun verlangte,\ndoch dem er wehrte - zuwider sich selbst -,\nallzu vertraut wagte die Trotzige,\ndas für sich zu vollbringen,\nBrünnhild' in brennender Schlacht.\nStreitvater strafte die Maid:\nin ihr Auge drückte er Schlaf;\nauf dem Felsen schläft sie fest:\nerwachen wird die Weihliche nur,\num einen Mann zu minnen als Weib.\nFrommten mir Fragen an sie?","translation":"You mean the Valkyrie, right?\nBrünnhild, the maiden?\nShe defied the storm conqueror,\nwhere he most strongly subdued himself:\nwhich required the leader of the battle to do,\nbut he resisted it - contrary to himself -\nThe defiant woman dared to trust too closely,\nto accomplish that for oneself\nBrünnhild' in a burning battle.\nThe feuding father punished the maid:\nHe pressed sleep into her eye;\nShe sleeps soundly on the rock:\nThe Holy One will only awaken,\nto love a man as a woman.\nDid I have any questions for her?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":55,"sourceLineCount":15},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"ist in Sinnen versunken und beginnt erst nach längerem Schweigen","translation":"is lost in thought and only begins after a long silence","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":70,"sourceLineCount":1}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Wirr wird mir, seit ich erwacht:","translatedTitle":"I've been feeling confused since I woke up:","participants":["ERDA","WANDERER"],"sourceStartIndex":71,"sourceLineCount":58,"turns":[{"speaker":"ERDA","speakerTranslation":"ERDA","original":"Wirr wird mir, seit ich erwacht:\nwild und kraus kreist die Welt!\nDie Walküre, der Wala Kind,\nbüsst' in Banden des Schlafs,\nals die wissende Mutter schlief?\nDer den Trotz lehrte, straft den Trotz?\nDer die Tat entzündet, zürnt um die Tat?\nDer die Rechte wahrt, der die Eide hütet,\nwehret dem Recht, herrscht durch Meineid? -\nLass mich wieder hinab!\nSchlaf verschliesse mein Wissen!","translation":"I've been feeling confused since I woke up:\nThe world revolves wildly and chaotically!\nThe Valkyrie, the Wala child,\nis punished in the bonds of sleep,\nwhen the knowing mother slept?\nDoes he who taught defiance punish defiance?\nDoes the one who instigates the act resent the act itself?\nHe who upholds rights, he who guards oaths,\nDoes it resist justice, does it rule through perjury?\nLet me down again!\nSleep closes my knowledge!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":71,"sourceLineCount":11},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Dich, Mutter, lass' ich nicht ziehn,\nda des Zaubers mächtig ich bin.\nUrwissend stachest du einst\nder Sorge Stachel in Wotans wagendes Herz:\nmit Furcht vor schmachvoll feindlichem Ende\nfüllt' ihn dein Wissen,\ndass Bangen band seinen Mut.\nBist du der Welt weisestes Weib,\nsage mir nun:\nwie besiegt die Sorge der Gott?","translation":"I won't let you go, Mother.\nbecause I am powerful in magic.\nWith primal knowledge, you once stabbed\nthe sting of worry in Wotan's daring heart:\nwith fear of a shameful, hostile end\nFill it with your knowledge,\nThat fear bound his courage.\nAre you the wisest woman in the world?\nNow tell me:\nHow does God conquer worry?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":82,"sourceLineCount":10},{"speaker":"ERDA","speakerTranslation":"ERDA","original":"Du bist - nicht was du dich nennst!\nWas kamst du, störrischer Wilder,\nzu stören der Wala Schlaf?","translation":"You are not what you call yourself!\nWhy did you come, stubborn savage?\nto disturb Wala's sleep?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":92,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Du bist - nicht, was du dich wähnst!\nUrmütter-Weisheit geht zu Ende:\ndein Wissen verweht vor meinem Willen.\nWeisst du, was Wotan will?","translation":"You are not what you think you are!\nThe wisdom of the ancient mothers is coming to an end:\nYour knowledge is blown away before my will.\nDo you know what Wotan wants?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":95,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Langes Schweigen","translation":"Long silence","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":99,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Dir Unweisen ruf' ich ins Ohr,\ndass sorglos ewig du nun schläfst!\nUm der Götter Ende grämt mich die Angst nicht,\nseit mein Wunsch es will!\nWas in des Zwiespalts wildem Schmerze\nverzweifelnd einst ich beschloss,\nfroh und freudig führe frei ich nun aus.\nWeiht' ich in wütendem Ekel\ndes Niblungen Neid schon die Welt,\ndem herrlichsten Wälsung\nweis' ich mein Erbe nun an.\nDer von mir erkoren, doch nie mich gekannt,\nein kühnester Knabe, bar meines Rates,\nerrang des Niblungen Ring.\nLiebesfroh, ledig des Neides,\nerlahmt an dem Edlen Alberichs Fluch;\ndenn fremd bleibt ihm die Furcht.\nDie du mir gebarst, Brünnhild',\nweckt sich hold der Held:\nwachend wirkt dein wissendes Kind\nerlösende Weltentat. -\nDrum schlafe nun du, schliesse dein Auge;\nträumend erschau' mein Ende!\nWas jene auch wirken,\ndem ewig Jungen weicht in Wonne der Gott.\nHinab denn, Erda! Urmütterfurcht!\nUrsorge!\nHinab! Hinab, zu ewigem Schlaf!","translation":"To you unwise people I call in your ear,\nMay you sleep carefree forever!\nThe end of the gods does not trouble me with fear.\nSince my wish wills it!\nWhat in the conflict's wild pain\nIn despair I once decided,\nGladly and joyfully I now carry out my task freely.\nI consecrated in furious disgust\nThe Nibelung's envy has already spread throughout the world,\nthe most glorious Wälsung\nI now bequeath my inheritance.\nThe one I chose, yet who never knew me,\na boldest boy, without my advice,\nwon the Ring of the Nibelungs.\nLoving and free from envy,\nweakens under the curse of the noble Alberich;\nFor fear remains foreign to him.\nThe one you bore me, Brünnhilde,\nThe hero awakens gently:\nYour knowing child appears alert.\nA redemptive world act. -\nSo now go to sleep, close your eyes;\nDreamingly behold my end!\nWhatever those effects may be,\nThe eternally young man yields in bliss to the god.\nDown then, Earth! Primordial Mother Fear!\nPrimary concern!\nDown! Down, to eternal sleep!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":100,"sourceLineCount":28},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Nachdem Erda bereits die Augen geschlossen hat und allmählich tiefer versunken ist, verschwindet sie jetzt gänzlich; auch die Höhle ist jetzt wiederum durchaus verfinstert. Monddämmerung erhellt die Bühne, der Sturm hat aufgehört","translation":"After Erda had already closed her eyes and gradually sunk deeper, she now disappears completely; the cave is once again completely darkened. Moonlight illuminates the scene, the storm has ceased.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":128,"sourceLineCount":1}]}]},{"number":2,"originalHeading":"ZWEITE SZENE","translatedHeading":"Second Scene","summary":"","sections":[{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Dort seh' ich Siegfried nahn.","translatedTitle":"There I see Siegfried approaching.","participants":["WANDERER","SIEGFRIED"],"sourceStartIndex":0,"sourceLineCount":75,"turns":[{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Dort seh' ich Siegfried nahn.","translation":"There I see Siegfried approaching.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":0,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er verbleibt in seiner Stellung an der Höhle. Siegfrieds Waldvogel flattert dem Vordergrunde zu. Plötzlich hält der Vogel in seiner Richtung ein, flattert ängstlich hin und her und verschwindet hastig dem Hintergrunde zu\ntritt rechts im Vordergrunde auf und hält an","translation":"He remains in his position by the cave. Siegfried's wood bird flutters towards the foreground. Suddenly, the bird stops in its direction, flutters anxiously back and forth, and hastily disappears into the background.\nappears on the right in the foreground and stops.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":1,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Mein Vöglein schwebte mir fort!\nMit flatterndem Flug und süssem Sang\nwies es mich wonnig des Wegs:\nnun schwand es fern mir davon!\nAm besten find' ich mir selbst nun den Berg:\nwohin mein Führer mich wies,\ndahin wandr' ich jetzt fort.","translation":"My little bird flew away from me!\nWith fluttering flight and sweet song\nIt blissfully showed me the way:\nNow it vanished far from me!\nI think the mountain is the best place for me now:\nwhere my guide showed me,\nThat is where I am now wandering off to.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":3,"sourceLineCount":7},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er schreitet weiter nach hinten\nin seiner Stellung an der Höhle verbleibend","translation":"He continues to step backwards\nremaining in his position at the cave","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":10,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Wohin, Knabe, heisst dich dein Weg?","translation":"Where, boy, will your path lead you?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":12,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"hält an und wendet sich um","translation":"stops and turns around","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":13,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Da redet's ja:\nwohl rät das mir den Weg.","translation":"There it is talking:\nThis will probably advise me on the way.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":14,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er tritt dem Wanderer näher","translation":"He approaches the hiker.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":16,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Einen Felsen such' ich,\nvon Feuer ist der umwabert:\ndort schläft ein Weib,\ndas ich wecken will.","translation":"I'm looking for a rock,\nIt is surrounded by fire:\nA woman is sleeping there,\nthat I want to wake up.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":17,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Wer sagt' es dir, den Fels zu suchen?\nWer, nach der Frau dich zu sehnen?","translation":"Who tells you to look for the rock?\nWho, after whom you yearn for the woman?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":21,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Mich wies ein singend Waldvöglein:\ndas gab mir gute Kunde.","translation":"A singing forest bird pointed me in the right direction:\nThat gave me good news.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":23,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Ein Vöglein schwatzt wohl manches;\nkein Mensch doch kann's verstehn.\nWie mochtest du Sinn dem Sang entnehmen?","translation":"A little bird chatters about many things;\nNo one can understand it.\nHow would you like to derive meaning from the song?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":25,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Das wirkte das Blut eines wilden Wurms,\nder mir vor Neidhöhl' erblasste:\nkaum netzt' es zündend die Zunge mir,\nda verstand ich der Vöglein Gestimm'.","translation":"It looked like the blood of a wild worm,\nwho paled before my eyes:\nIt barely wets my tongue with a spark,\nThen I understood the voice of the little birds.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":28,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Erschlugst den Riesen du,\nwer reizte dich,\nden starken Wurm zu bestehn?","translation":"You slew the giant,\nwho provoked you,\nto survive the strong worm?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":32,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Mich führte Mime, ein falscher Zwerg;\ndas Fürchten wollt' er mich lehren:\nzum Schwertstreich aber,\nder ihn erschlug,\nreizte der Wurm mich selbst;\nseinen Rachen riss er mir auf.","translation":"Mime, a false dwarf, led me;\nHe wanted to teach me fear:\nBut to the sword stroke,\nwho killed him,\nThe worm irritated me;\nHe ripped his throat open.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":35,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Wer schuf das Schwert so scharf und hart,\ndass der stärkste Feind ihm fiel?","translation":"Who created the sword so sharp and hard?\nthat his strongest enemy fell to him?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":41,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Das schweisst' ich mir selbst,\nda's der Schmied nicht konnte:\nschwertlos noch wär' ich wohl sonst.","translation":"I welded that myself,\nbecause the blacksmith couldn't:\nI would probably still be swordless otherwise.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":43,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Doch, wer schuf die starken Stücken,\ndaraus das Schwert du dir geschweisst?","translation":"But who created the powerful pieces?\nFrom that, you welded yourself the sword?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":46,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Was weiss ich davon?\nIch weiss allein,\ndass die Stücke mir nichts nützten,\nschuf ich das Schwert mir nicht neu.","translation":"What do I know about that?\nI know only,\nthat the pieces were of no use to me,\nI did not recreate the sword for myself.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":48,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"bricht in ein freudig gemütliches Lachen aus","translation":"bursts into a joyful, cozy laugh","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":52,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Das mein' ich wohl auch!","translation":"That's what I think too!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":53,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er betrachtet Siegfried wohlgefällig\nverwundert","translation":"He regards Siegfried approvingly.\nsurprised","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":54,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Was lachst du mich aus?\nAlter Frager! Hör' einmal auf;\nlass mich nicht länger hier schwatzen!\nKannst du den Weg mir weisen, so rede:\nvermagst du's nicht, so halte dein Maul!","translation":"Why are you laughing at me?\nOld questioner! Stop it!\nDon't let me chatter here any longer!\nIf you can show me the way, then speak:\nIf you can't do it, then shut your mouth!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":56,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Geduld, du Knabe! Dünk' ich dich alt,\nso sollst du Achtung mir bieten.","translation":"Patience, you boy! Do I think you're old?\nYou should show me respect.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":61,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Das wär' nicht übel!\nSolang' ich lebe,\nstand mir ein Alter stets im Wege;\nden hab' ich nun fortgefegt.\nStemmst du dort länger steif dich mir entgegen,\nsieh dich vor, sag' ich,","translation":"That wouldn't be bad!\nAs long as I live,\nMy age was always an obstacle for me;\nI've now swept him away.\nIf you stand stiffly facing me there for longer,\nWatch out, I say,","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":63,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"mit entsprechender Gebärde","translation":"with appropriate gesture","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":69,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"dass du wie Mime nicht fährst!","translation":"that you don't drive like Mime!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":70,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er tritt noch näher an den Wanderer heran","translation":"He steps even closer to the hiker.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":71,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Wie siehst du denn aus?\nWas hast du gar für 'nen grossen Hut?\nWarum hängt er dir so ins Gesicht?","translation":"So, what do you look like?\nWhat a big hat you have!\nWhy is he hanging in your face like that?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":72,"sourceLineCount":3}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Das ist so Wand'rers Weise,","translatedTitle":"That is the way of the wanderer,","participants":["WANDERER","SIEGFRIED"],"sourceStartIndex":75,"sourceLineCount":74,"turns":[{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"immer ohne seine Stellung zu verlassen","translation":"always without leaving his position","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":75,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Das ist so Wand'rers Weise,\nwenn dem Wind entgegen er geht.","translation":"That is the way of the wanderer,\nwhen he goes against the wind.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":76,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"immer näher ihn betrachtend","translation":"looking closer and closer to him","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":78,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Doch darunter fehlt dir ein Auge!\nDas schlug dir einer gewiss schon aus,\ndem du zu trotzig den Weg vertratst?\nMach dich jetzt fort,\nsonst könntest du leicht\ndas andere auch noch verlieren.","translation":"But you're missing one eye!\nSomeone has certainly already refused to do that for you,\nwhose path you defiantly pursued?\nGet out of here now,\notherwise you could easily\nand lose the other one too.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":79,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Ich seh', mein Sohn, wo du nichts weisst,\nda weisst du dir leicht zu helfen.\nMit dem Auge, das als andres mir fehlt,\nerblickst du selber das eine,\ndas mir zum Sehen verblieb.","translation":"I see, my son, where you know nothing,\nYou can easily help yourself with that.\nWith the eye that I lack as the other,\nDo you yourself see that one thing?\nthat was left for me to see.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":85,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"der sinnend zugehört hat, bricht jetzt unwillkürlich in helles Lachen aus","translation":"The person who had been listening thoughtfully now involuntarily bursts into bright laughter.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":90,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Zum Lachen bist du mir lustig!\nDoch hör', nun schwatz' ich nicht länger:\ngeschwind, zeig' mir den Weg,\ndeines Weges ziehe dann du;\nzu nichts andrem acht' ich dich nütz':\ndrum sprich, sonst spreng' ich dich fort!","translation":"You're so funny!\nBut listen, I won't babble any longer:\nQuickly, show me the way,\nThen go your own way;\nI consider you useless for nothing else:\nSpeak up, or I'll blow you up!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":91,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"weich","translation":"soft","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":97,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Kenntest du mich, kühner Spross,\nden Schimpf spartest du mir!\nDir so vertraut,\ntrifft mich schmerzlich dein Dräuen.\nLiebt' ich von je deine lichte Art,\nGrauen auch zeugt' ihr mein zürnender Grimm.\nDem ich so hold bin, Allzuhehrer,\nheut' nicht wecke mir Neid:\ner vernichtete dich und mich!","translation":"Did you know me, bold sprout,\nYou spared me the insult!\nYou are so familiar with me\nYour threats pain me deeply.\nI have always loved your bright nature,\nMy angry wrath also begets horror.\nTo whom I am so devoted, All-Giving One,\nDon't awaken envy in me today:\nHe destroyed you and me!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":98,"sourceLineCount":9},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Bleibst du mir stumm, störrischer Wicht?\nWeich' von der Stelle,\ndenn dorthin, ich weiss,\nführt es zur schlafenden Frau.\nSo wies es mein Vöglein,\ndas hier erst flüchtig entfloh.","translation":"Will you remain silent to me, you stubborn wretch?\nMove away from the spot,\nbecause there, I know,\nIt leads to the sleeping woman.\nThat's how my little bird showed me,\nthat only escaped briefly.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":107,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Es wird schnell wieder ganz finster\nin Zorn ausbrechend und in gebieterischer Stellung","translation":"It will quickly become very dark again.\nerupting in anger and in a commanding posture","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":113,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Es floh dir zu seinem Heil!\nDen Herrn der Raben erriet es hier:\nweh' ihm, holen sie's ein!\nDen Weg, den es zeigte,\nsollst du nicht ziehn!","translation":"It fled to your salvation!\nIt guessed the Lord of the Ravens here:\nWoe to him, let's catch up with him!\nThe path it showed,\nYou shouldn't pull!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":115,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"tritt mit Verwunderung in trotziger Stellung zurück","translation":"resigns in a defiant stance, surprised,","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":120,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Hoho! Du Verbieter!\nWer bist du denn,\ndass du mir wehren willst?","translation":"Hoho! You prohibitionist!\nWho are you, then,\nThat you want to defend me?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":121,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Fürchte des Felsens Hüter!\nVerschlossen hält meine Macht die schlafende Maid:\nwer sie erweckte, wer sie gewänne,\nmachtlos macht' er mich ewig!\nEin Feuermeer umflutet die Frau,\nglühende Lohe umleckt den Fels:\nwer die Braut begehrt,\ndem brennt entgegen die Brunst.","translation":"Fear the Rock Keeper!\nMy power keeps the sleeping maiden locked away:\nwhoever awakened them, whoever gained them,\nHe renders me powerless forever!\nA sea of ​​fire engulfs the woman,\nGlowing flames licked around the rock:\nwho desires the bride,\nThe lust burns in opposition to that.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":124,"sourceLineCount":8},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er winkt mit dem Speere nach der Felsenhöhe","translation":"He waves his spear towards the rocky height.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":132,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Blick' nach der Höh'!\nErlugst du das Licht?\nEs wächst der Schein,\nes schwillt die Glut;\nsengende Wolken, wabernde Lohe\nwälzen sich brennend und prasselnd herab:\nein Lichtmeer umleuchtet dein Haupt:","translation":"Look towards the heights!\nDo you feel the light?\nThe illusion grows,\nThe embers swell;\nscorching clouds, shimmering flames\nrolling down, burning and crackling:\nA sea of ​​light illuminates your head:","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":133,"sourceLineCount":7},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Mit wachsender Helle zeigt sich von der Höhe des Felsens her ein wabernder Feuerschein","translation":"As the light grows brighter, a shimmering glow of fire appears from the top of the rock.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":140,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"bald frisst und zehrt dich zündendes Feuer.\nZurück denn, rasendes Kind!","translation":"Soon, igniting fire will devour and consume you.\nBack then, you raging child!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":141,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Zurück, du Prahler, mit dir!","translation":"Back with you, you braggart!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":143,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er schreitet weiter, der Wanderer stellt sich ihm entgegen","translation":"He continues walking, the hiker confronts him.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":144,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Dort, wo die Brünste brennen,\nzu Brünnhilde muss ich dahin!","translation":"Where the fires burn,\nI must go there to see Brünnhilde!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":145,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"Fürchtest das Feuer du nicht,","translation":"Do you not fear the fire?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":147,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"den Speer vorhaltend","translation":"holding the spear","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":148,"sourceLineCount":1}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"so sperre mein Speer dir den Weg!","translatedTitle":"So let my spear block your way!","participants":["WANDERER","SIEGFRIED"],"sourceStartIndex":149,"sourceLineCount":25,"turns":[{"speaker":"WANDERER","speakerTranslation":"WANDERER","original":"so sperre mein Speer dir den Weg!\nNoch hält meine Hand der Herrschaft Haft:\ndas Schwert, das du schwingst,\nzerschlug einst dieser Schaft:\nnoch einmal denn zerspring' es am ew'gen Speer!","translation":"So let my spear block your way!\nMy hand still holds the master's hand:\nthe sword you wield,\nThis shaft once shattered:\nOnce more, for may it shatter on the eternal spear!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":149,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er streckt den Speer vor\ndas Schwert ziehend","translation":"He extends the spear\ndrawing the sword","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":154,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Meines Vaters Feind! Find' ich dich hier?\nHerrlich zur Rache geriet mir das!\nSchwing' deinen Speer:\nin Stücken spalt' ihn mein Schwert!\nEr haut dem Wanderer mit einem Schlage den Speer in zwei Stücken; ein Blitzstrahl fährt daraus nach der Felsenhöhe zu, wo von nun an der bisher mattere Schein in immer helleren Feuerflammen zu lodern beginnt. Starker Donner, der schnell sich abschwächt, begleitet den Schlag. Die Speerstücken rollen zu des Wanderers Füssen. Er rafft sie ruhig auf","translation":"My father's enemy! Will I find you here?\nI got my revenge brilliantly!\nSwing your spear:\nMy sword will split him to pieces!\nWith a single blow, he shatters the wanderer's spear in two; a bolt of lightning shoots from it towards the rocky heights, where the previously dim light begins to blaze into ever brighter flames. A loud rumble of thunder, which quickly subsides, accompanies the blow. The spear fragments roll at the wanderer's feet. He calmly gathers them up.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":156,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"WANDERER\nzurückweichend","translation":"WALKER\nretreating","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":161,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Zieh hin! Ich kann dich nicht halten!","translation":"Move on! I can't stop you!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":163,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er verschwindet plötzlich in völliger Finsternis","translation":"He suddenly disappears into complete darkness.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":164,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Mit zerfocht'ner Waffe wich mir der Feige?","translation":"Did the coward leave me with his weapon broken?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":165,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Die wachsende Helle der immer tiefer sich senkenden Feuerwolken trifft Siegfrieds Blick","translation":"Siegfried's gaze falls upon the growing brightness of the ever-lowering fire clouds.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":166,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Ha! Wonnige Glut! Leuchtender Glanz!\nStrahlend nun offen steht mir die Strasse.\nIm Feuer mich baden!\nIm Feuer zu finden die Braut -\nHoho! Hahei!\nJetzt lock' ich ein liebes Gesell!","translation":"Ha! Blissful glow! Radiant brilliance!\nThe street now lies brightly open before me.\nBathe in fire!\nFinding the bride in the fire -\nHoho! Hahei!\nNow I'll lure a lovely fellow!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":167,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Siegfried setzt sein Horn an und stürzt, seine Lockweise blasend, sich in das wogende Feuer, welches sich, von der Höhe herabdringend, nun auch über den Vordergrund ausbreitet. Siegfried, den man bald nicht mehr erblickt, scheint sich nach der Höhe zu entfernen. Hellstes Leuchten der Flammen. Danach beginnt die Glut zu erbleichen und löst sich allmählich in ein immer feineres, wie durch die Morgenröte beleuchtetes Gewölk auf","translation":"Siegfried raises his horn and, blowing his call, plunges into the surging fire, which, descending from the heights, now spreads across the foreground. Siegfried, soon out of sight, seems to be retreating towards the heights. The flames glow brightest. Then the embers begin to fade and gradually dissolve into an ever-finer cloud, illuminated as if by the dawn.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":173,"sourceLineCount":1}]}]},{"number":3,"originalHeading":"DRITTE SZENE","translatedHeading":"Third Scene","summary":"","sections":[{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Das immer zarter gewordene Gewölk hat sich in einen feinen Nebelschleier von rosiger Färbung aufgelöst und zer","translatedTitle":"The ever-thinning cloud has dissolved into a fine veil of rosy mist and now parts in such a way that the fragr","participants":["Stage direction","SIEGFRIED"],"sourceStartIndex":0,"sourceLineCount":71,"turns":[{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Das immer zarter gewordene Gewölk hat sich in einen feinen Nebelschleier von rosiger Färbung aufgelöst und zerteilt sich nun in der Weise, dass der Duft sich gänzlich nach oben verzieht und endlich nur noch den heiteren, blauen Tageshimmel erblicken lässt, während am Saume der nun sichtbar werdenden Felsenhöhe - ganz die gleiche Szene wie im dritten Aufzug der \"Walküre\" - ein morgenrötlicher Nebelschleier haften bleibt, welcher zugleich an die in der Tiefe noch lodernde Zauberlohe erinnert. Die Anordnung der Szene ist durchaus dieselbe wie am Schlusse der \"Walküre\": im Vordergrunde, unter der breitästigen Tanne, liegt Brünnhilde in vollständiger, glänzender Panzerrüstung, mit dem Helm auf dem Haupte, den langen Schild über sich gedeckt, in tiefem Schlafe","translation":"The ever-thinning cloud has dissolved into a fine veil of rosy mist and now parts in such a way that the fragrance rises entirely upwards, finally revealing only the bright, blue daytime sky, while at the edge of the now visible rocky height—exactly the same scene as in the third act of \"Die Walküre\"—a reddish veil of mist clings, simultaneously recalling the magic flame still blazing in the depths below. The arrangement of the scene is precisely the same as at the end of \"Die Walküre\": in the foreground, beneath the broad-branched fir tree, Brünnhilde lies in deep sleep, clad in full, gleaming armor, her helmet upon her head, her long shield covered over her.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":0,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"gelangt von aussen her auf den felsigen Saum der Höhe und zeigt sich dort zuerst nur mit dem Oberleibe: so blickt er lange staunend um sich","translation":"He approaches the rocky edge of the height from the outside and at first reveals himself only with his upper body: he gazes around him in wonder for a long time.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":1,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Selige Öde auf sonniger Höh'!","translation":"Blessed solitude on a sunny height!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":2,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er steigt vollends herauf und betrachtet, auf einem Felsensteine des hinteren Abhanges stehend, mit Verwunderung die Szene. Er blickt zur Seite in den Tann und schreitet etwas vor","translation":"He climbs all the way up and, standing on a rock on the far slope, surveys the scene in wonder. He glances sideways into the fir forest and steps forward a little.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":3,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Was ruht dort schlummernd im schattigen Tann?\nEin Ross ist's, rastend in tiefem Schlaf!","translation":"What lies slumbering there in the shady fir trees?\nIt's a horse, resting in a deep sleep!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":4,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Langsam näher kommend, hält er verwundert an, als er noch aus einiger Entfernung Brünnhildes Gestalt wahrnimmt","translation":"Slowly approaching, he stops in surprise when he perceives Brünnhilde's figure from some distance away.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":6,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Was strahlt mir dort entgegen?\nWelch glänzendes Stahlgeschmeid?\nBlendet mir noch die Lohe den Blick?","translation":"What is shining back at me from there?\nWhat gleaming steel jewelry!\nIs the flame still blinding my vision?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":7,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er tritt näher hinzu","translation":"He steps closer.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":10,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Helle Waffen! Heb' ich sie auf?","translation":"Bright weapons! Should I pick them up?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":11,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er hebt den Schild ab und erblickt Brünnhildes Gestalt, während ihr Gesicht jedoch noch zum grossen Teil vom Helm verdeckt ist","translation":"He lifts his shield and sees Brünnhilde's figure, although her face is still largely hidden by her helmet.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":12,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Ha! In Waffen ein Mann:\nwie mahnt mich wonnig sein Bild!\nDas hehre Haupt drückt wohl der Helm?\nLeichter würd' ihm, löst' ich den Schmuck.","translation":"Ha! A man in arms:\nHow blissfully his image reminds me!\nIs the helmet pressing down on the noble head?\nIt would be easier for him if I removed the jewelry.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":13,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Vorsichtig löst er den Helm und hebt ihn der Schlafenden vom Haupte ab: langes lockiges Haar bricht hervor. Siegfried erschrickt","translation":"Carefully, he loosens the helmet and lifts it from the sleeping woman's head: long, curly hair bursts out. Siegfried is startled.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":17,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Ach! Wie schön!","translation":"Oh! How lovely!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":18,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er bleibt in den Anblick versunken","translation":"He remains engrossed in the sight.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":19,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Schimmernde Wolken säumen in Wellen\nden hellen Himmelssee;\nleuchtender Sonne lachendes Bild\nstrahlt durch das Wogengewölk!","translation":"Shimmering clouds fringe the landscape in waves.\nthe bright sky lake;\nbright sun smiling image\nshines through the cloudy waves!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":20,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er neigt sich tiefer zu der Schlafenden hinab","translation":"He leans down further towards the sleeping woman.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":24,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Von schwellendem Atem schwingt sich die Brust:\nbrech' ich die engende Brünne?","translation":"The chest rises and falls with each swelling breath:\nShould I break the narrow well?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":25,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er versucht mit grosser Behutsamkeit, die Brünne zu lösen","translation":"He is trying to loosen the well with great care.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":27,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Komm, mein Schwert, schneide das Eisen!","translation":"Come, my sword, cut the iron!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":28,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er zieht sein Schwert, durchschneidet mit zarter Vorsicht die Panzerringe zu beiden Seiten der ganzen Rüstung und hebt dann die Brünne und die Schienen ab, so dass nun Brünnhilde in einem weichen weiblichen Gewande vor ihm liegt. Er fährt erschreckt und staunend auf","translation":"He draws his sword, carefully cuts through the ring armor on both sides of the entire suit of armor, and then lifts off the mail and greaves, so that Brünnhilde now lies before him in a soft, feminine garment. He jumps up, startled and amazed.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":29,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Das ist kein Mann!","translation":"That's not a man!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":30,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er starrt mit höchster Aufgeregtheit auf die Schlafende hin","translation":"He stares at the sleeping woman with extreme excitement.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":31,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Brennender Zauber zückt mir ins Herz;\nfeurige Angst fasst meine Augen:\nmir schwankt und schwindelt der Sinn!","translation":"A burning magic stirs my heart;\nFiery fear engulfs my eyes:\nMy mind is wavering and dizzy!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":32,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er gerät in höchste Beklemmung","translation":"He becomes extremely anxious.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":35,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Wen ruf' ich zum Heil, dass er mir helfe?\nMutter! Mutter! Gedenke mein!","translation":"To whom shall I call for salvation, that he may help me?\nMother! Mother! Remember me!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":36,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er sinkt, wie ohnmächtig, an Brünnhildes Busen. Langes Schweigen. Dann fährt er seufzend auf","translation":"He collapses, as if unconscious, against Brünnhilde's breast. A long silence. Then he sits up with a sigh.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":38,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Wie weck' ich die Maid,\ndass sie ihr Auge mir öffne?\nDas Auge mir öffne?\nBlende mich auch noch der Blick?\nWagt' es mein Trotz?\nErtrüg' ich das Licht?\nMir schwebt und schwankt\nund schwirrt es umher!\nSehrendes Sehnen zehrt meine Sinne;\nam zagenden Herzen zittert die Hand!\nWie ist mir Feigem?\nIst dies das Fürchten?\nO Mutter! Mutter! Dein mutiges Kind!\nIm Schlafe liegt eine Frau:\ndie hat ihn das Fürchten gelehrt!\nWie end' ich die Furcht?\nWie fass' ich Mut?\nDass ich selbst erwache,\nmuss die Maid mich erwecken!","translation":"How do I wake the maid,\nthat she would open her eye to me?\nOpen my eye?\nAm I also blinded by their gaze?\nDoes my defiance dare?\nCan I bear the light?\nI feel suspended and wavering\nand it whizzes around!\nA burning longing consumes my senses;\nThe hand trembles on the timid heart!\nHow do I feel about being a coward?\nIs this what fear is?\nO Mother! Mother! Your brave child!\nA woman lies asleep:\nShe taught him to be afraid!\nHow do I end the fear?\nHow do I find courage?\nThat I myself awaken,\nThe maid must awaken me!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":39,"sourceLineCount":19},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Indem er sich der Schlafenden von neuem nähert, wird er wieder von zarteren Empfindungen an ihren Anblick gefesselt. Er neigt sich tiefer hinab","translation":"As he approaches the sleeping woman anew, he is once again captivated by more tender feelings directed at her. He bends down lower.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":58,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Süss erbebt mir ihr blühender Mund.\nWie mild erzitternd mich Zagen er reizt!\nAch! Dieses Atems wonnig warmes Gedüft!","translation":"Her blooming mouth trembles sweetly at me.\nHow mildly he tempts me with trembling fear!\nAh! The blissfully warm scent of your breath!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":59,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"wie in Verzweiflung","translation":"as if in despair","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":62,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Erwache! Erwache! Heiliges Weib!","translation":"Awake! Awake! Holy Woman!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":63,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er starrt auf sie hin","translation":"He stares at her","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":64,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Sie hört mich nicht.","translation":"She can't hear me.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":65,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"gedehnt mit gepresstem, drängendem Ausdruck","translation":"stretched with a strained, urgent expression","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":66,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"So saug' ich mir Leben\naus süssesten Lippen,\nsollt' ich auch sterbend vergehn!","translation":"That's how I suck my life dry.\nfrom the sweetest lips,\nEven if I should perish in death!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":67,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er sinkt, wie ersterbend, auf die Schlafende und heftet mit geschlossenen Augen seine Lippen auf ihren Mund. Brünnhilde schlägt die Augen auf. Siegfried fährt auf und bleibt vor ihr stehen. Brünnhilde richtet sich langsam zum Sitze auf. Sie begrüsst mit feierlichen Gebärden der erhobenen Arme ihre Rückkehr zur Wahrnehmung der Erde und des Himmels","translation":"He sinks, as if dying, upon the sleeping woman and, with closed eyes, presses his lips to hers. Brünnhilde opens her eyes. Siegfried starts and stands before her. Brünnhilde slowly rises to her seat. With solemn gestures of raised arms, she welcomes her return to the perception of earth and heaven.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":70,"sourceLineCount":1}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Heil dir, Sonne!","translatedTitle":"Hail to you, sun!","participants":["BRÜNNHILDE","SIEGFRIED"],"sourceStartIndex":71,"sourceLineCount":63,"turns":[{"speaker":"BRÜNNHILDE","speakerTranslation":"BRÜNNHILDE","original":"Heil dir, Sonne!\nHeil dir, Licht!\nHeil dir, leuchtender Tag!\nLang war mein Schlaf;\nich bin erwacht.\nWer ist der Held, der mich erweckt'?","translation":"Hail to you, sun!\nHail to you, Light!\nHail to you, bright day!\nMy sleep was long;\nI have woken up.\nWho is the hero who awakens me?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":71,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"von ihrem Blicke und ihrer Stimme feierlich ergriffen, steht wie festgebannt","translation":"Solemnly moved by her gaze and her voice, he stands as if spellbound.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":77,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Durch das Feuer drang ich,\ndas den Fels umbrann;\nich erbrach dir den festen Helm:\nSiegfried bin ich, der dich erweckt'.","translation":"I penetrated through the fire,\nthat burned the rock;\nI vomited up your hard helmet:\nI am Siegfried, who awakens you.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":78,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"hoch aufgerichtet sitzend","translation":"sitting upright","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":82,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"BRÜNNHILDE","speakerTranslation":"BRÜNNHILDE","original":"Heil euch, Götter!\nHeil dir, Welt!\nHeil dir, prangende Erde!\nZu End' ist nun mein Schlaf;\nerwacht, seh' ich:\nSiegfried ist es, der mich erweckt!","translation":"Hail to you, gods!\nHail to you, world!\nHail to you, splendid earth!\nMy sleep is now over;\nI wake up and see:\nIt is Siegfried who awakens me!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":83,"sourceLineCount":6},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"in erhabenste Verzückung ausbrechend","translation":"breaking out into the most sublime rapture","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":89,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"O Heil der Mutter, die mich gebar;\nHeil der Erde, die mich genährt!\nDass ich das Aug' erschaut,\ndas jetzt mir Seligem lacht!","translation":"O salvation to the mother who bore me;\nHail to the earth that nourished me!\nThat I beheld the eye,\nwho now laughs with blessedness!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":90,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"mit grösster Bewegtheit","translation":"with the greatest agitation","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":94,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"BRÜNNHILDE","speakerTranslation":"BRÜNNHILDE","original":"O Heil der Mutter, die dich gebar!\nHeil der Erde, die dich genährt!\nNur dein Blick durfte mich schau'n,\nerwachen durft' ich nur dir!","translation":"O Hail to the mother who bore you!\nHail to the earth that nourished you!\nOnly your gaze was allowed to look at me,\nI was only allowed to awaken to you!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":95,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Beide bleiben voll strahlenden Entzückens in ihren gegenseitigen Anblick verloren","translation":"Both remain lost in radiant delight at each other's gaze.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":99,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"BRÜNNHILDE","speakerTranslation":"BRÜNNHILDE","original":"O Siegfried! Siegfried! Seliger Held!\nDu Wecker des Lebens, siegendes Licht!\nO wüsstest du, Lust der Welt,\nwie ich dich je geliebt!\nDu warst mein Sinnen,\nmein Sorgen du!\nDich Zarten nährt' ich,\nnoch eh' du gezeugt;\nnoch eh' du geboren,\nbarg dich mein Schild:\nso lang' lieb' ich dich, Siegfried!","translation":"Oh Siegfried! Siegfried! Blessed hero!\nYou awakener of life, victorious light!\nOh, if you knew, joy of the world,\nHow I ever loved you!\nYou were my senses,\nYou are my worry!\nI nourished you, tender one,\neven before you were conceived;\neven before you were born,\nMy shield hid you:\nI'll love you for so long, Siegfried!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":100,"sourceLineCount":11},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"leise und schüchtern","translation":"quiet and shy","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":111,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"So starb nicht meine Mutter?\nSchlief die minnige nur?","translation":"So, my mother didn't die like that?\nWas the lovely lady only asleep?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":112,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"lächelnd, freundlich die Hand nach ihm ausstreckend","translation":"smiling, reaching out his hand to him in a friendly manner","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":114,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"BRÜNNHILDE","speakerTranslation":"BRÜNNHILDE","original":"Du wonniges Kind!\nDeine Mutter kehrt dir nicht wieder.\nDu selbst bin ich,\nwenn du mich Selige liebst.\nWas du nicht weisst,\nweiss ich für dich;\ndoch wissend bin ich\nnur - weil ich dich liebe!\nO Siegfried! Siegfried! Siegendes Licht!\nDich liebt' ich immer;\ndenn mir allein erdünkte Wotans Gedanke.\nDer Gedanke, den ich nie nennen durfte;\nden ich nicht dachte, sondern nur fühlte;\nfür den ich focht, kämpfte und stritt;\nfür den ich trotzte dem, der ihn dachte;\nfür den ich büsste, Strafe mich band,\nweil ich nicht ihn dachte und nur empfand!\nDenn der Gedanke - dürftest du's lösen! -\nmir war er nur Liebe zu dir!","translation":"You delightful child!\nYour mother will not return to you.\nI am you,\nif you love me, Blessed One.\nWhat you don't know,\nI know for you;\nBut I am aware\nOnly – because I love you!\nO Siegfried! Siegfried! Victorious light!\nI always loved you;\nFor Wotan's thought occurred to me alone.\nThe thought I was never allowed to mention;\nwhich I didn't think, but only felt;\nfor whom I fought, struggled, and argued;\nfor whom I defied the one who thought of him;\nfor which I atoned, punishment bound me,\nBecause I didn't think of him, I only felt him!\nBecause the thought – could you solve it! –\nTo me, he was only love for you!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":115,"sourceLineCount":19}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Wie Wunder tönt, was wonnig du singst;","translatedTitle":"How wonderful it sounds, what you blissfully sing;","participants":["SIEGFRIED","BRÜNNHILDE"],"sourceStartIndex":134,"sourceLineCount":74,"turns":[{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Wie Wunder tönt, was wonnig du singst;\ndoch dunkel dünkt mich der Sinn.\nDeines Auges Leuchten seh' ich licht;\ndeines Atems Wehen fühl' ich warm;\ndeiner Stimme Singen hör' ich süss:\ndoch was du singend mir sagst,\nstaunend versteh' ich's nicht.\nNicht kann ich das Ferne sinnig erfassen,\nwenn alle Sinne dich nur sehen und fühlen!\nMit banger Furcht fesselst du mich:\ndu Einz'ge hast ihre Angst mich gelehrt.\nDen du gebunden in mächtigen Banden,\nbirg meinen Mut mir nicht mehr!","translation":"How wonderful it sounds, what you blissfully sing;\nBut the meaning seems obscure to me.\nI see the light in your eyes;\nI feel the warmth of your breath;\nI hear your voice singing sweetly:\nBut what you say to me while singing,\nI am amazed and don't understand it.\nI cannot meaningfully grasp the distant,\nWhen all your senses can only see and feel you!\nYou bind me with dreadful fear:\nYou alone have taught me their fear.\nThe one you bound in mighty chains,\nDon't hide my courage from me anymore!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":134,"sourceLineCount":13},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er verweilt in grosser Aufregung, sehnsuchtsvollen Blick auf sie heftend\nwendet sanft das Haupt zur Seite und richtet ihren Blick nach dem Tann","translation":"He lingers in great excitement, his longing gaze fixed on her.\nShe gently turns her head to the side and directs her gaze towards the fir tree.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":147,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"BRÜNNHILDE","speakerTranslation":"BRÜNNHILDE","original":"Dort seh' ich Grane,\nmein selig Ross:\nwie weidet er munter,\nder mit mir schlief!\nMit mir hat ihn Siegfried erweckt.","translation":"There I see Grane,\nmy blessed horse:\nHow cheerfully he grazes,\nwho slept with me!\nSiegfried awakened him with my help.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":149,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"in der vorigen Stellung verbleibend","translation":"remaining in the previous position","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":154,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Auf wonnigem Munde weidet mein Auge:\nin brünstigem Durst doch brennen die Lippen,\ndass der Augen Weide sie labe!","translation":"My eye feasts upon a delightful mouth:\nMy lips burn with raging thirst,\nthat the eyes may feast upon them!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":155,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"deutet ihm mit der Hand nach ihren Waffen, die sie gewahrt","translation":"She gestures to him with her hand towards her weapons, which she notices.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":158,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"BRÜNNHILDE","speakerTranslation":"BRÜNNHILDE","original":"Dort seh' ich den Schild,\nder Helden schirmte;\ndort seh' ich den Helm,\nder das Haupt mir barg:\ner schirmt, er birgt mich nicht mehr!","translation":"There I see the sign,\nwho protected the heroes;\nThere I see the helmet,\nwho hid my head:\nHe shields me, he no longer protects me!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":159,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Eine selige Maid versehrte mein Herz;\nWunden dem Haupte schlug mir ein Weib:\nich kam ohne Schild und Helm!","translation":"A blessed maiden wounded my heart;\nA woman inflicted wounds on my head:\nI arrived without a shield or helmet!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":164,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"mit gesteigertem Wehmut","translation":"with heightened melancholy","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":167,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"BRÜNNHILDE","speakerTranslation":"BRÜNNHILDE","original":"Ich sehe der Brünne prangenden Stahl:\nein scharfes Schwert schnitt sie entzwei;\nvon dem maidlichen Leibe löst' es die Wehr:\nich bin ohne Schutz und Schirm,\nohne Trutz ein trauriges Weib!","translation":"I see the steel gleaming on the fountain:\nA sharp sword cut her in two;\nThe weapon was released from the maiden's body:\nI am without protection or shield,\nWithout defiance, a sad woman!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":168,"sourceLineCount":5},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Durch brennendes Feuer fuhr ich zu dir!\nNicht Brünne noch Panzer barg meinen Leib:\nnun brach die Lohe mir in die Brust.\nEs braust mein Blut in blühender Brunst;\nein zehrendes Feuer ist mir entzündet:\ndie Glut, die Brünnhilds Felsen umbrann,\ndie brennt mir nun in der Brust!\nO Weib, jetzt lösche den Brand!\nSchweige die schäumende Glut!","translation":"I traveled to you through burning fire!\nNeither pylons nor tanks sheltered my body:\nNow the flames broke into my chest.\nMy blood rushes in blooming rage;\nA consuming fire has been lit within me:\nthe embers that engulfed Brünnhild's rocks,\nIt's burning in my chest now!\nO woman, now extinguish the fire!\nSilence the foaming embers!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":173,"sourceLineCount":9},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er hat sie heftig umfasst: sie springt auf, wehrt ihm mit der höchsten Kraft der Angst, und entflieht nach der anderen Seite","translation":"He grabbed her tightly: she jumped up, resisted him with the greatest force of fear, and fled to the other side.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":182,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"BRÜNNHILDE","speakerTranslation":"BRÜNNHILDE","original":"Kein Gott nahte mir je!\nDer Jungfrau neigten scheu sich die Helden:\nheilig schied sie aus Walhall!\nWehe! Wehe!\nWehe der Schmach, der schmählichen Not!\nVerwundet hat mich, der mich erweckt!\nEr erbrach mir Brünne und Helm:\nBrünnhilde bin ich nicht mehr!","translation":"No god ever approached me!\nThe heroes bowed shyly to the maiden:\nShe departed from Valhalla in a holy manner!\nWoe is me! Woe is me!\nWoe to the disgrace, the shameful misery!\nHe who awakened me has wounded me!\nHe vomited up my mail and helmet:\nI am no longer Brünnhilde!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":183,"sourceLineCount":8},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Noch bist du mir die träumende Maid:\nBrünnhildes Schlaf brach ich noch nicht.\nErwache, sei mir ein Weib!","translation":"You are still the dreaming maiden to me:\nI have not yet broken Brünnhilde's sleep.\nAwake, be a woman to me!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":191,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"in Betäubung","translation":"under anesthesia","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":194,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"BRÜNNHILDE","speakerTranslation":"BRÜNNHILDE","original":"Mir schwirren die Sinne,\nmein Wissen schweigt:\nsoll mir die Weisheit schwinden?","translation":"My senses are spinning,\nMy knowledge is silent:\nShould my wisdom fade away?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":195,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Sangst du mir nicht,\ndein Wissen sei\ndas Leuchten der Liebe zu mir?","translation":"Didn't you sing to me,\nbe your knowledge\nThe glow of love for me?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":198,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"vor sich hinstarrend","translation":"staring ahead","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":201,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"BRÜNNHILDE","speakerTranslation":"BRÜNNHILDE","original":"Trauriges Dunkel trübt meinen Blick;\nmein Auge dämmert, das Licht verlischt:\nNacht wird's um mich.\nAus Nebel und Grau'n\nwindet sich wütend ein Angstgewirr:\nSchrecken schreitet und bäumt sich empor!","translation":"A sad darkness clouds my vision;\nMy eyes grow dim, the light fades:\nNight falls around me.\nOut of fog and dread\nA tangled web of fear writhes angrily:\nTerror strides and rears up!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":202,"sourceLineCount":6}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Nacht umfängt gebund'ne Augen.","translatedTitle":"Night envelops bound eyes.","participants":["SIEGFRIED","BRÜNNHILDE"],"sourceStartIndex":208,"sourceLineCount":69,"turns":[{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Sie birgt heftig die Augen mit beiden Händen\nindem er ihr sanft die Hände von den Augen löst","translation":"She violently covers her eyes with both hands.\nby gently removing her hands from her eyes","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":208,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Nacht umfängt gebund'ne Augen.\nMit den Fesseln schwindet das finstre Grau'n.\nTauch' aus dem Dunkel und sieh:\nsonnenhell leuchtet der Tag!","translation":"Night envelops bound eyes.\nWith the shackles, the dark horror fades.\nEmerge from the darkness and see:\nThe day shines brightly!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":210,"sourceLineCount":4},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"in höchster Ergriffenheit","translation":"deeply moved","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":214,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"BRÜNNHILDE","speakerTranslation":"BRÜNNHILDE","original":"Sonnenhell leuchtet der Tag meiner Schmach!\nO Siegfried! Siegfried!\nSieh' meine Angst!","translation":"The day of my disgrace shines brightly!\nOh Siegfried! Siegfried!\nLook at my fear!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":215,"sourceLineCount":3},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Ihre Miene verrät, dass ihr ein anmutiges Bild vor die Seele tritt, von welchem ab sie den Blick mit Sanftmut wieder auf Siegfried richtet","translation":"Her expression betrays that a graceful image appears before her mind, from which she gently turns her gaze back to Siegfried.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":218,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"BRÜNNHILDE","speakerTranslation":"BRÜNNHILDE","original":"Ewig war ich, ewig bin ich,\newig in süss sehnender Wonne,\ndoch ewig zu deinem Heil!\nO Siegfried! Herrlicher! Hort der Welt!\nLeben der Erde! Lachender Held!\nLass, ach lass, lasse von mir!\nNahe mir nicht mit der wütenden Nähe!\nZwinge mich nicht\nmit dem brechenden Zwang,\nzertrümmre die Traute dir nicht!\nSahst du dein Bild im klaren Bach?\nHat es dich Frohen erfreut?\nRührtest zur Woge das Wasser du auf,\nzerflösse die klare Fläche des Bachs:\ndein Bild sähst du nicht mehr,\nnur der Welle schwankend Gewog'!\nSo berühre mich nicht,\ntrübe mich nicht!\nEwig licht lachst du selig dann\naus mir dir entgegen,\nfroh und heiter ein Held!\nO Siegfried! Leuchtender Spross!\nLiebe dich und lasse von mir:\nvernichte dein Eigen nicht!","translation":"I was eternal, I am eternal,\neternally in sweetly yearning bliss,\nbut forever for your salvation!\nO Siegfried! Glorious one! Treasure of the world!\nLife of Earth! Laughing hero!\nLet me, oh let me, let me go!\nDo not approach me with angry closeness!\nDon't force me\nwith the breaking compulsion,\nDon't let your courage be destroyed!\nDid you see your image in the clear stream?\nDid it please you, Frohen?\nYou stirred the water to the wave,\nthe clear surface of the stream dissolved:\nYou would no longer see your image,\nonly the wave-wave-like sway!\nSo don't touch me,\nDon't upset me!\nEternally light, you laugh blissfully then\nfrom me towards you\nA cheerful and bright hero!\nO Siegfried! Shining offspring!\nLove yourself and let me tell you:\nDo not destroy what is yours!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":219,"sourceLineCount":24},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Dich lieb' ich: o liebtest mich du!\nNicht hab' ich mehr mich:\no, hätte ich dich!\nEin herrlich Gewässer wogt vor mir;\nmit allen Sinnen seh' ich nur sie,\ndie wonnig wogende Welle.\nBrach sie mein Bild, so brenn' ich nun selbst,\nsengende Glut in der Flut zu kühlen;\nich selbst, wie ich bin,\nspring' in den Bach:\no, dass seine Wogen mich selig verschlängen,\nmein Sehnen schwänd' in der Flut!\nErwache, Brünnhilde!\nWache, du Maid!\nLache und lebe, süsseste Lust!\nSei mein! Sei mein! Sei mein!","translation":"I love you: oh, you loved me!\nI no longer have myself:\nOh, if only I had you!\nA magnificent body of water surges before me;\nWith all my senses I see only her,\nthe blissfully undulating wave.\nIf she broke my image, then I myself will burn.\nto cool the scorching embers in the flood;\nmyself, as I am,\nJump into the stream:\nOh, that its waves might blissfully engulf me,\nMay my longing vanish in the flood!\nAwaken, Brünnhilde!\nWatch out, maiden!\nLaugh and live, sweetest joy!\nBe mine! Be mine! Be mine!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":243,"sourceLineCount":16},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"sehr innig","translation":"very intimate","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":259,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"BRÜNNHILDE","speakerTranslation":"BRÜNNHILDE","original":"O Siegfried! Dein war ich von je!","translation":"O Siegfried! I was yours forever!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":260,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"feurig","translation":"fiery","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":261,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Warst du's von je, so sei es jetzt!","translation":"If you ever were, so be it now!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":262,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"BRÜNNHILDE","speakerTranslation":"BRÜNNHILDE","original":"Dein werd' ich ewig sein!","translation":"I will be yours forever!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":263,"sourceLineCount":1},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Was du sein wirst, sei es mir heut'!\nFasst dich mein Arm,\numschling' ich dich fest;\nschlägt meine Brust\nbrünstig die deine;\nzünden die Blicke,\nzehren die Atem sich;\nAug' in Auge, Mund an Mund:\ndann bist du mir,\nwas bang du mir warst und wirst!\nDann brach sich die brennende Sorge,\nob jetzt Brünnhilde mein?","translation":"Whatever you will be, be it to me today!\nIf my arm catches you,\nI'll hug you tightly;\nMy chest beats\nlustfully yours;\ntheir eyes ignite,\nTheir breath grows heavy;\nEye to eye, mouth to mouth:\nthen you are mine,\nHow much you meant to me and will remain to me!\nThen the burning worry broke,\nIs Brünnhilde mine now?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":264,"sourceLineCount":12},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er hat sie umfasst","translation":"He embraced them","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":276,"sourceLineCount":1}]},{"type":"Passage","incipitOnly":true,"sourceTitlesOnly":true,"threeLineOutline":true,"originalTitle":"Ob jetzt ich dein?","translatedTitle":"Is this you?","participants":["BRÜNNHILDE","SIEGFRIED"],"sourceStartIndex":277,"sourceLineCount":58,"turns":[{"speaker":"BRÜNNHILDE","speakerTranslation":"BRÜNNHILDE","original":"Ob jetzt ich dein?\nGöttliche Ruhe rast mir in Wogen;\nkeuschestes Licht lodert in Gluten:\nhimmlisches Wissen stürmt mir dahin,\nJauchzen der Liebe jagt es davon!\nOb jetzt ich dein?\nSiegfried! Siegfried!\nSiehst du mich nicht?\nWie mein Blick dich verzehrt,\nerblindest du nicht?\nWie mein Arm dich presst,\nentbrennst du mir nicht?\nWie in Strömen mein Blut entgegen dir stürmt,\ndas wilde Feuer, fühlst du es nicht?\nFürchtest du, Siegfried,\nfürchtest du nicht das wild wütende Weib?","translation":"Is this you?\nDivine peace surges through me in waves;\nThe most chaste light blazes in gluten:\nHeavenly knowledge rushes towards me,\nThe shouts of love chase it away!\nIs this you?\nSiegfried! Siegfried!\nCan't you see me?\nHow my gaze consumes you,\nWon't you go blind?\nHow my arm squeezes you,\nDon't you ignite my passion?\nAs my blood rushes towards you in torrents,\nThe wild fire, don't you feel it?\nAre you afraid, Siegfried?\nAre you not afraid of the wildly angry woman?","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":277,"sourceLineCount":16},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Sie umfasst ihn heftig\nin freudigem Schreck","translation":"She grips him tightly\nin joyful terror","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":293,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Ha! Wie des Blutes Ströme sich zünden,\nwie der Blicke Strahlen sich zehren,\nWie die Arme brünstig sich pressen, -\nkehrt mir zurück mein kühner Mut,\nund das Fürchten, ach!\nDas ich nie gelernt,\ndas Fürchten, das du mich kaum gelehrt:\ndas Fürchten, - mich dünkt -\nich Dummer vergass es nun ganz!","translation":"Ha! Like streams of blood igniting,\nhow the rays of gaze consume each other,\nHow the arms press themselves lustfully, -\nMy bold courage returns to me,\nAnd the fear, alas!\nThat I never learned,\nthe fear that you scarcely taught me:\nthe fear, - it seems to me -\nI, being the fool I am, completely forgot!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":295,"sourceLineCount":9},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Er hat bei den letzten Worten Brünnhilde unwillkürlich losgelassen\nim höchsten Liebesjubel wild auflachend","translation":"He involuntarily let go of Brünnhilde at her last words.\nlaughing wildly in the highest jubilation of love","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":304,"sourceLineCount":2},{"speaker":"BRÜNNHILDE","speakerTranslation":"BRÜNNHILDE","original":"O kindischer Held!\nO herrlicher Knabe!\nDu hehrster Taten töriger Hort!\nLachend muss ich dich lieben,\nlachend will ich erblinden,\nlachend zugrunde gehn!\nFahr' hin, Walhalls leuchtende Welt!\nZerfall in Staub deine stolze Burg!\nLeb' wohl, prangende Götterpracht!\nEnd' in Wonne, du ewig Geschlecht!\nZerreisst, ihr Nornen, das Runenseil!\nGötterdämm'rung, dunkle herauf!\nNacht der Vernichtung, neble herein!\nMir strahlt zur Stunde Siegfrieds Stern;\ner ist mir ewig, ist mir immer,\nErb' und Eigen, ein' und all':\nleuchtende Liebe, lachender Tod!","translation":"Oh childish hero!\nOh, what a splendid boy!\nYou foolish repository of noblest deeds!\nI must love you while laughing,\nI want to go blind laughing,\nGoing to death laughing!\nGo there, Valhalla's shining world!\nYour proud castle crumbles to dust!\nFarewell, magnificent splendor of the gods!\nEnd in bliss, you eternal race!\nTear apart, you Norns, the rune rope!\nTwilight of the gods, dark dawn!\nNight of destruction, fog in!\nSiegfried's star shines for me at this hour;\nHe is eternal to me, is always to me,\nInheritance and possession, one and all:\nRadiant love, laughing death!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":306,"sourceLineCount":17},{"speaker":"SIEGFRIED","speakerTranslation":"SIEGFRIED","original":"Lachend erwachst du Wonnige mir:\nBrünnhilde lebt, Brünnhilde lacht!\nHeil dem Tage, der uns umleuchtet!\nHeil der Sonne, die uns bescheint!\nHeil der Welt, der Brünnhilde lebt!\nSie wacht, sie lebt,\nsie lacht mir entgegen.\nPrangend strahlt mir Brünnhildes Stern!\nSie ist mir ewig, ist mir immer,\nErb' und Eigen, ein' und all':\nleuchtende Liebe, lachender Tod!","translation":"Laughing, you blissful one awakens to me:\nBrünnhilde lives, Brünnhilde laughs!\nHail to the day that illuminates us!\nHail to the sun that shines upon us!\nHail to the world, Brünnhilde lives!\nShe is awake, she is alive,\nShe laughs at me.\nBrünnhilde's star shines brilliantly for me!\nShe is eternal to me, is always to me,\nInheritance and possession, one and all:\nRadiant love, laughing death!","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":323,"sourceLineCount":11},{"speaker":"Stage direction","speakerTranslation":"Stage direction","original":"Brünnhilde stürzt sich in Siegfrieds Arme. Der Vorhang fällt","translation":"Brünnhilde throws herself into Siegfried's arms. The curtain falls.","literalText":true,"sourceStartIndex":334,"sourceLineCount":1}]}]}];
